\f0\b Analyze the output
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\tx940\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	1.	}SMAUG generates 2 \'93.csv\'94 files, one containing all snakes and has the total filament and junction point counts at the bottom that has the suffix \'93snakeslengthoutput_RAW.csv\'94 and the other contains the manually verified tracks that has the suffix \'93snakeslength_output.csv\'94\
{\listtext	2.	}For each track, the filament length and average intensity are presented for each frame. The output also includes the start and end points for the line(s) fit to the filament, the slope of the best fit line(s), the y-intercept, the slope of the change in intensity over time, and the y-intercept of the intensity best fit line(s). \
{\listtext	3.	}To calculate the elongation rate, the \'93slope\'94 value should be converted from pixels per frame to subunits per second. The conversion factor for our imaging setup is:\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li1440\fi-1440\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	} slope * (0.1088 \'b5m / pixel / 5 seconds / frame) * 370 subunits / \'b5m\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\

\f0\b\fs28 Troubleshooting
\f1\b0\fs22 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	1.	}Deform and/or tracking may take a long time, or demand too much memory. Consider cropping the image or reducing the number of frames tracked to reduce the memory required for processing\
{\listtext	2.	}Oversegmentation may be reduced by increasing the stretch factor\
{\listtext	3.	}Undersegmentation may be reduced by decreasing the stretch factor\
{\listtext	4.	}Too much noise or poorly initialized filaments may be optimized by adjusting the ridge threshold\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
